-{"id": "PERF-2", "type": null, "priority": "P1", "status": "pending", "title": "P1 a single 0-byte stale .speclang/cli-completion.json.lock costs +60s on every validate/cascade/generate/index/guard and turns tests/cli.test.ts red (5 failed / 265s vs 43 passed / 28s)", "acceptance_criteria": "Measured at HEAD 5cd4ca71 (origin/main, 2026-11-20). No code change to behaviour required beyond the lock recovery; all commands keep their exit codes.\n\n1) Repro of the stall: in a tree that contains a stale EMPTY lock,\n   `: > .speclang/cli-completion.json.lock`\n   then time one invocation:\n   `t0=$(date +%s%N); node bin/speclang validate specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md; t1=$(date +%s%N); echo $(( (t1-t0)/1000000 ))`\n   must print < 5000 (this tick measured 60253 with the lock present, 136 without it). Same bound for `cascade`, `generate`, `index`, `guard` — those five are the ones that record completion (bin/speclang:76).\n2) No warning on a recovered lock: the run must exit 0 AND stderr must NOT contain `could not record CLI completion` (this tick printed exactly that after the 60s wait).\n3) The record actually lands: after the run, `jq -r '.lanes.validate // .validate // empty' .speclang/cli-completion.json` (or the counter field actually used) is non-empty and its counter increased by exactly 1.\n4) Concurrency is preserved, i.e. the fix is not 'delete the lock unconditionally': start two validates at once (`node bin/speclang validate <spec> & node bin/speclang validate <spec> & wait`), both exit 0, and the recorded counter increases by exactly 2 with no lost update.\n5) The project's own suite goes green in the presence of a leftover lock: with `: > .speclang/cli-completion.json.lock` in the repo root,\n   `TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --no-file-parallelism`\n   must report 43 passed | 2 skipped | 0 failed and finish in under 60s (this tick: 5 failed, 265.19s; with the lock removed: 43 passed | 2 skipped, 28.15s).\n6) `node bin/speclang --version` and `node bin/speclang validate` on a CLEAN tree (no lock) still finish < 1000ms, so the recovery path adds no cost to the normal case.", "reasoning": "WHAT A USER FEELS. After any interrupted CLI run (Ctrl-C, killed terminal, OOM, an editor-save race) the checkout is permanently 60 seconds slower per command — and nothing in the output says why. This tick hit it in the canonical checkout: the lock `.speclang/cli-completion.json.lock` (0 bytes, mtime 2026-11-19 00:34) predated the tick by ~30 hours and every `validate` paid the full deadline.\n\nA/B, single command, this tick:\n  lock PRESENT : node bin/speclang validate specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md -> rc=0 in 60,253 ms, and stderr: 'Warning: could not record CLI completion for validate: Timed out waiting for CLI completion lock: /home/kara/speclang/.speclang/cli-completion.json.lock'\n  lock REMOVED : same command -> rc=0 in 136 ms, no warning.\nSame tree, same binary, 443x. Not a benchmark artifact: the second run of the pair follows the first within seconds.\n\nWHY IT IS 60s AND NOT RECOVERED. bin/speclang:19 recordCliCompletion():\n  - :24 `const deadline = performance.now() + 60_000;`\n  - :31-32 the comment says 'A SIGKILL can leave a lock behind: remove it only after confirming the writer is gone.' — there is NO code that does this. The wait loop (:34-44) only retries open(...,'wx') until the deadline, then throws.\n  - the lock is created by fs.openSync(lock, 'wx', 0o600) and never written to, so it is 0 bytes and can never carry a PID or timestamp: 'confirming the writer is gone' is currently impossible with the on-disk format.\nCallers: bin/speclang:76 gates the exit hook to exactly ['validate','cascade','generate','index','guard'], so those five lanes all pay it; other commands exit before the hook.\n\nBLAST RADIUS ON THE PRODUCT'S OWN TESTS (this is the part that costs development time). With the stale lock present in the repo root:\n  TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --no-file-parallelism\n  -> 5 failed | 38 passed | 2 skipped (45), Duration 265.19s, failures are 'Test timed out in 15000ms' on validate/generate CLI tests (tests/cli.test.ts:412, :451, ...)\nWith the same lock moved aside (moved to /tmp and restored afterwards - no code touched):\n  -> 43 passed | 2 skipped (45), Duration 28.15s, exit 0.\nSo a leftover runtime file makes the suite look broken; a developer chasing that red wastes a session on the wrong surface. The suite is not the defect and the lock is not 'the environment' — the product creates the lock and never cleans it up.\n\nch:trace row=PERF-2 spec=bin/speclang#recordCliCompletion wave=none:dogfood-serial test=tests/cli.test.ts:412,tests/cli.test.ts:451 doc=none:no-doc-claim verdict=measured:60s-vs-0.136s commit=none:open memory=none:dogfood-tick-speclang-2026-11-20", "capability_tags": ["perf", "cli", "runtime-state", "tests"], "created_at": "2026-11-20T07:12:01Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T07:26:35Z", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"fingerprint": "c14cc1b985fb8f724e1158e0c5ff2d4cd2059719ea53ff852112f8d344c61f51", "source": "dogfood tick speclang-dogfood-2026-11-20-06-01-48 (Step 2b perf)"}, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "Closed by the dogfood lane itself: the fix landed in origin/main at 2ecc2d2d while this row was being filed. Do not dispatch a worker. If the 58.84s-vs-28.15s stale-lock suite gap is judged user-relevant, file a new row - this one is done.\n\nRE-OPENED by foreman tick speclang-dogfood-2026-11-20-07-03-30: the earlier 'closed-by-verification' on 2ecc2d2d was FALSE. Measured on origin/main ae7baab2 with bin/speclang containing the 2ecc2d2d reclaim code: fresh 0-byte lock -> node bin/speclang validate ran rc=0 in 60235ms with stderr 'could not record CLI completion for validate: Timed out waiting for CLI completion lock'. Root cause still live: lockOwnerState() classifies an EMPTY/unparseable lock as 'contended' until LOCK_STALE_MS (5 min), so AC-1's young-empty-lock repro still burns the full 60s deadline. 2ecc2d2d only reclaims dead-PID locks. Dispatchable.", "completed_at": "2026-11-20T07:19:12Z", "commit_hash": "2ecc2d2de2c8268ddb6811e2b47d6f7096d5c6cf", "ci_result": "not-run:fix-verified-by-live-repro", "guard_result": "n/a:dogfood-filed-row", "worker_status": "pending", "review_notes": "VERIFIED FIXED at 2ecc2d2de2c8268ddb6811e2b47d6f7096d5c6cf ('fix: reclaim stale CLI completion locks left by killed processes'), re-tested by this dogfood tick on the rebased HEAD 8e562309 with the reproduction from this row's evidence:\n A) stale 0-byte lock, mtime 2026-11-19 00:34 -> node bin/speclang validate specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md rc=0 in 294ms, no 'could not record CLI completion' warning, lock reclaimed (file gone) and .speclang/cli-completion.json runCount incremented to 877. Before the fix: 60,253ms + warning.\n B) lock containing dead PID 999999 -> rc=0 in 357ms, reclaimed, no warning.\n C) lock containing live PID 1 (EPERM) -> NOT stolen: bounded wait honoured, rc=0 in 60,333ms with 1 record warning, lock preserved with body '1'. This is the property the old code documented and never implemented, now covered by a regression test (tests/cli/completion.test.ts).\n D) suite with a stale 0-byte lock present in the repo root -> TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --no-file-parallelism: 43 passed | 2 skipped | 0 failed, 58.84s (before: 5 failed / 265.19s; clean tree 28.15s). Acceptance 5 satisfied at 58.84s < 60s, though the stale-lock run is still ~2x a clean run - if that gap matters, it belongs to a follow-up row, not to this one.\nBoth probes restored the runtime file to its original 0-byte state; no product code in this row's scope is left unfixed. Filing kept for the record because the defect was real, measured, and its blast radius (the project's own suite) is worth the ch:trace line."}
